
@startuml
title AppWrapper Process Lifecycle

actor "Client (Model)" as Client
participant "AppWrapper (app_wrapperd)" as AppWrapper
participant "Console Utility" as Util

== Start request ==
Client -> AppWrapper : Start(appId, args, env, options)
AppWrapper -> AppWrapper : Validates arguments,\ncreates process object,\ngenerates unique object path

== Process launch ==
alt Normal process
    AppWrapper -> Util : spawn(cmd, args, {cwd, env, stdio: ['pipe','pipe','pipe']})
else Interactive (PTY)
    AppWrapper -> Util : pty.spawn(cmd, args, {cwd, env, cols, rows})
end

== Set up event handlers ==
alt Normal process
    AppWrapper -> AppWrapper : Set stdout.on('data'),\nstderr.on('data'),\nchild.on('close'),\nchild.on('error')
else Interactive (PTY)
    AppWrapper -> AppWrapper : Set pty.on('data'),\npty.on('exit')
end

== Notify started ==
AppWrapper -> Client : Started(pid)

== Output forwarding loop ==
loop While process is running
    Util -> AppWrapper : stdout/stderr data
    AppWrapper -> Client : Output(stream, data)
end

== Command handling ==
Client -> AppWrapper : Stop(path)
AppWrapper -> Util : Sends signal (SIGTERM)\nor kills process

Client -> AppWrapper : SendInput(path, data)
AppWrapper -> Util : Writes to stdin (child.stdin.write()\nor pty.write())

== Process termination ==
Util -> AppWrapper : close/exit event (code, signal)
AppWrapper -> Client : Exited(code, signal)
AppWrapper -> AppWrapper : Keeps process object active\nfor a while, then removes it

== Error handling ==
Util -> AppWrapper : error event
AppWrapper -> Client : Error(message)

@enduml

